---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/10-07/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/10-07/interactions.json';
const a='/equipment/10-07/',spec='https://www.sutter.com/micromanipulation/mp-285',manual='https://www.sutter.com/hubfs/WEB%20-%20Manuals/MP-285_OpMan_Joystick_BasicOp.pdf?hsLang=en#page=13',stage='https://www.neurolabparts.com/407-thickbox_default/mp-285-motorized-micromanipulator-.jpg';
const display=x=>Object.entries(x??{}).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+(Array.isArray(v)?'['+v.join(', ')+']':String(v))).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="Sutter MP-285 inert coordinate stage" subtitle="" description="Inspect a metric MP-285/T and exercise a purely virtual inert cube coordinate transform." wide={true}>
<article id="mp" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/10-07/">← Equipment 10-07</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#mp-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">10-07 / Sutter MP-285/T / Virtual inert datum cube</p><h2>Sutter MP-285</h2><p>Apply virtual stage travel and see how it maps into an inert cube’s sample coordinate frame. At 90° yaw, a local +3 mm X request becomes +3 mm in sample Y. Try +40 mm to see local X stop at +12.5 mm.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect stage and control replica</h3><div id="mp-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Front','Stage','Control'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="mp-xr" type="button" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div><canvas id="mp-model" aria-label="Orbitable scaled MP-285 with three axis carriages, input prop, and inert datum cube"></canvas><p id="mp-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">Click the virtual joystick knob to apply a pose or its red, green or brass button for +1 mm in X, Y or Z. The sample marker uses the transformed result; slide animation shows local travel, not a change in the physical mount angle.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Request a virtual position</h3><form id="mp-form" novalidate><div class="e-fields">{[['xMm','Local X (mm)',3,100],['yMm','Local Y (mm)',0,100],['zMm','Local Z (mm)',0,100],['yawDeg','Sample yaw (degrees)',90,180]].map(([k,t,v,max])=><label>{t}<input name={k} type="number" min={-max} max={max} step="any" value={v}/></label>)}</div><div class="e-row"><button id="mp-move" class="e-run" type="submit">Apply virtual pose</button><button id="mp-limit" type="button">Try +40 mm</button><button id="mp-reset" type="button">Reset</button></div></form>
<div class="e-row">{['X','Y','Z'].map(k=><button type="button" id={'mp-nudge-'+k}>{'+1 mm '+k}</button>)}</div><p id="mp-status" role="status">No command applied.</p></section></div>
<section class="e-card"><h3>03 · Read local and sample coordinates</h3><p id="mp-result" role="status">No pose calculated.</p><div class="e-row"><button id="mp-json" disabled>Export pose JSON</button></div><p>The stage request is clipped independently on X, Y and Z to a centered ±12.5 mm range. The sample frame uses positive yaw about +Z, right-handed, Z up. Sample position is <strong>t</strong> + <strong>R</strong><sub>Z</sub>(θ)<strong>q</strong>, with a fixed example datum offset (4, −2, 1) mm. Export preserves applied and requested local travel, blocked axes, sample position in metres and millimetres, and revisions. <a href={a+'example-pose.json'}>Example pose</a>.</p></section>
<section><h3>Selected reference configuration</h3><div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original tabletop MP-285 controller, stage and joystick rendering"/><figcaption>Original tabletop MP-285/T model. Controller enclosure and mechanism use the <a href={spec}>Sutter specification and primary product photo</a>. The input prop’s color targets are added for this virtual station, not literal controller labels.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original three-axis stage construction and datum cube"/><figcaption>Overview of the three draft slide meshes and inert marker; the source <a href={stage}>mechanical unit photograph</a> and <a href={manual}>Sutter joystick manual, figures 2-1 through 2-3</a> inform visible placement and component classes.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Geometry</th><th>Published / model value</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mechanical unit</td><td>110 × 150 × 160 mm</td><td>Manufacturer reported nominal envelope, axes assigned in this model.</td></tr><tr><td>Tabletop controller</td><td>406 × 273 × 96 mm</td><td>Reported width × depth × height.</td></tr><tr><td>Local travel</td><td>25 mm per axis</td><td>Manufacturer’s rounded metric figure; centered home is assumed. Reported inch and rounded metric values are not treated as exact equivalents.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Controller details, joystick dimensions and cube mount are originals or estimates. Collision detection, backlash, validation against measured accuracy, hardware I/O, speed and real biological positioning are not modeled. This is an independent rigid-coordinate check, not a physical calibration.</p></section>
<section id="mp-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{display(x.expected)}</td><td>{display(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'sutter-mp285.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Named targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles and {m.draws} draw primitives; optional WebXR, physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/10-07/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#mp header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#mp h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#mp section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#mp button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#mp button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#mp-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#mp-chart{width:100%;max-height:16rem}.e-over{overflow:auto}#mp table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#mp td,#mp th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#mp figure{margin:0}#mp img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.e-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.e-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
#mp caption{text-align:left}#mp input,#mp select,#mp button{min-width:0}#mp .e-hint{font-size:.92rem}</style>
